\subsection{E1b: held-out linear tests (pre-registered)}
\label{sec:heldout}

\paragraph{Set-up and pre-registration.}
E1b changes everything that E1 could have tuned: $n=d=24$, $\sigma_k$ evenly spaced from $1.5$ to $0.5$ and $c_k=0.92^k\sigma_k$, encoder scale $a_0=10^{-3}$, gradient descent with step $0.1$.
Before any run we committed the rank predicted for each of the \EoneBRuns{} runs by the race criterion, its general form (\cref{app:more}), \cref{cor:alpha1}, Tian et al.'s basin criterion and the two baselines, with \EoneBCritAll{} pass/fail criteria (\texttt{results/e1b/prediction.json}); nothing was fitted afterwards.
The rank is read at convergence (unchanged over the last fifth of training; \EoneBAlignedConverged{} of gradient-descent runs converged); for $\lambda>0$ it is final in all but \EoneBLongChanged{} of \EoneBLongRuns{} checked runs (at $\lambda=0$ a horizon rank); \EoneBCritPass{} of the \EoneBCritAll{} criteria pass (\cref{tab:e1b}, \cref{app:details}).

\paragraph{The race predicts the rank on held-out statistics.}
On the \EoneBAlignedRuns{} runs with aligned statistics (a $p_0\times\lambda$ phase grid, EMA rate $\times$ predictor learning rate, and depth), the race classifies \EoneBAlignedModeAcc{} of directions, gives the exact rank in \EoneBAlignedExact{} of runs with mean absolute error \EoneBAlignedMae{}, and predicts complete collapse correctly in \EoneBAlignedCollapse{}; the initial window misses by \EoneBAlignedWindowMae{} directions and the static bound by \EoneBAlignedBoundMae{}.
On the phase grid (\cref{fig:e1b}) the exact-rank rate is \EoneBGridExact{} (error \EoneBGridMae{}; \cref{cor:alpha1}: \EoneBGridCorExact{} of \EoneBGridCorN{} runs), and the grid shows both effects of weight decay that the static threshold misses: at $p_0=0.5$ and $\lambda=\EoneBGridLams$ the measured rank is $\EoneBGridRanksHalf$ against the predicted $\EoneBGridPredHalf$, so weight decay first rescues directions and then removes them; and complete collapse sets in at a pre-registered $\lambda_c=\EoneBLamCollapseTenth$, $\EoneBLamCollapseHalf$ and $\EoneBLamCollapseOne$ for $p_0=0.1$, $0.5$ and $1$, against the static $\EoneBStaticLam$; the boundary misses \EoneBGridCollapseMisses{} of \EoneBGridCells{} cells.
In the balanced regime Tian et al.'s basin criterion and \cref{cor:alpha1} are exact in \EoneBBalancedExact{} of \EoneBBalancedRuns{} runs; without the stop-gradient or a predictor all \EoneBNosgRuns{} runs collapse, as predicted.
The general criterion, for random Gaussian predictors and non-commuting statistics, has error \EoneBGeneralMae{} and exact rank in \EoneBGeneralExact{} of \EoneBGeneralRuns{} runs (static bound \EoneBGeneralBoundMae{}).

\paragraph{Where it fails.}
Entering depth only through the clock, the race over-predicts the rank of deep predictors by $\approx1$ (error \EoneBDepthMae{}, \EoneBDepthFalsePos{} false survivals, \EoneBDepthFalseNeg{} missed); a post-hoc correction of the capture amplitude (App.~\ref{app:more}) passed a second pre-registered test on new statistics (E1c, \EoneCDeepRuns{} runs, $L=2$--$4$): error \EoneCMae{} against \EoneCMaeDepthOne{}, never over-predicting but conservative at $L=4$ (\cref{app:details}).
The EMA sign test fails narrowly: \EoneBEmaSignAgree{} of \EoneBEmaSignOf{} predicted changes have the measured sign, including the regime reversal of \cref{sec:heuristics}.
Under AdamW (\cref{app:more}) the rank is nearer the static bound (error \EoneBAdamBoundMae{}) than the race (\EoneBAdamRaceMae{}), but insensitivity to $a_0$ fails by \EoneBAdamWzeroMaxDiff{} and only \EoneBAdamConverged{} of \EoneBAdamRuns{} runs converge: at most partly supported.

\subsection{E2: masking (pre-registered)}
\label{sec:e2e3}
\label{sec:e2}

\paragraph{Set-up.}
The data are a Gaussian field on a cycle of $n=d=64$ sites (correlation $0.7^{\mathrm{distance}}$), with context and target complementary under a mask, which fixes $\Sigma_c=\Sigma\circ G$ and $\Sigma_{tc}=\Sigma\circ F$ (\cref{sec:heuristics}).
Cyclic masks (Bernoulli, one block, four blocks) make both circulant, so the race applies per frequency; a non-wrapping block needs the general form. Over $r\in\{0.1,\dots,0.9\}$, four $\lambda$ from $3\cdot10^{-4}$ to $10^{-2}$, $p_0\in\{0.25,0.5\}$ and 3 seeds we train by population gradient descent, by SGD with sampled masks, with a tanh encoder, with an exploratory two-layer encoder and without a predictor (\cref{app:details}).
Predictions for all \EtwoRuns{} runs and \EtwoCritAll{} criteria were committed first; \EtwoCritPass{} pass (\cref{tab:e2}).

\paragraph{Results.}
With the statistics the masks leave, the race classifies \EtwoCycFreqAcc{} of frequencies and has rank error \EtwoCycMae{} at $t_{\mathrm{end}}$ on the \EtwoCycRuns{} cyclic-mask runs (\EtwoLongMae{} against the rank at $t=\EtwoLongT$, \EtwoLongSmallMae{} at $\lambda=3\cdot10^{-4}$), against \EtwoCycWindowMae{} for the initial window and \EtwoCycBoundMae{} for the static bound (\cref{fig:e2}); its general form has \EtwoNcMae{} for non-wrapping blocks (bound \EtwoNcBoundMae{}), and SGD stays within \EtwoSgdMae{} of the population prediction.
The measured maximum matches the predicted one within a grid step in all \EtwoPeakProfiles{} profiles, but in \EtwoPeakEdge{} the predicted maximum reaches the grid edge; of the \EtwoNonmonoPred{} (Bernoulli) profiles predicted to fall again \EtwoNonmonoConf{} do (one keeps rank \EtwoMissMeas{} at $r=0.9$, as the exact flow does; predicted \EtwoMissPred{}), so that criterion fails.
Without a predictor, heavy Bernoulli masking makes directions grow in all \EtwoNopredGrowth{} configurations where App.~\ref{app:more} predicts it.
With a tanh encoder the race holds for block masks (error \EtwoTanhBlockMae{}, post hoc) but not for Bernoulli ones (\EtwoTanhBernMae{}), whose rank keeps rising after the race; the two-layer encoder misses by \EtwoMlpMae{} (Spearman \EtwoMlpSpearman{}).

\subsection{E3: a vision JEPA}
\label{sec:e3}
E3 is a transfer test on an I-JEPA-style ViT on CIFAR-10, which is not linear and does not start near collapse, in two arms: P follows the I-JEPA recipe (AdamW, EMA target), T is theory-aligned (SGD, stop-gradient copy target, decay on every parameter).
For \EthreeConfigs{} one-factor configurations (3 seeds) we registered the epoch-20 count of online-token covariance directions predicted from each run's step-0 drive, self-prediction and decay rates over the schedule (App.~\ref{app:details}): the analogue of the initial window, not of the race.
In Arm T the count falls with weight decay (\cref{fig:e3}; \EthreeTwdMeas{} for $\lambda=0,\dots,0.1$, rule \EthreeTwdPred{}) and the rule orders the configurations (Spearman \EthreeRankT{}, carried by the weight-decay sweep), but it places the transition $\EthreeLocFactor\times$ too high (registered: $2\times$), and under AdamW it fails (\EthreeRankP{}).
Weight decay, not the predictor or the target, sets Arm T's collapse: at $\lambda=0.01$ every predictor and target variant ends at \EthreeTvariants{} directions, and no registered intervention crosses the collapse line (\EthreeCfourCross{} of \EthreeCfourCrossOf{}: no rescue lifts a collapsed run, no break collapses a healthy one).
In Arm P all four mask settings lower the count (to \EthreePmaskRange{}, from \EthreePbase{}) where the rule registered no change; the signs for predictor learning rate and depth fail, the count rises with the EMA rate against the registered null, and no run without stop-gradient collapses completely by epoch 20 (\cref{tab:e3}); the 50-epoch collapse flags are right (\EthreeFullFlags{} of 3).
